<h2 id="sec-2">How We Chose</h2>
<p>Our evaluation focused on real-world usability: mist output consistency, coverage area, noise level (under 30 dB for bedroom use), build quality, ease of cleaning, design aesthetics, and value for money.</p>
<h2 id="sec-3">Top Picks Reviewed</h2>
<h3>1. URPOWER 2nd Edition — Best Value</h3>
<p>The URPOWER 2nd Edition remains the bestselling ultrasonic diffuser. At under $26, it delivers consistent mist across its 300ml tank, covering rooms up to 300 sq ft. The whisper-quiet operation (under 30 dB) makes it perfect for bedrooms. The auto-shutoff feature activates when water runs low.</p>
<div style="background:#F7F4EF;border-left:3px solid #C9A962;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin:1.5rem 0;border-radius:0 8px 8px 0"><p style="margin:0;font-size:0.95rem"><strong>Best for:</strong> First-time diffuser users, bedrooms, and budget-conscious buyers.</p></div>
<h3>2. ASAKUKI Premium — Best Large Capacity</h3>
<p>The ASAKUKI Premium stands out with its generous 500ml tank and 16-hour runtime on intermittent mode. The bamboo wood grain finish adds elegance, and the top-fill design makes refilling effortless without removing the lid.</p>
<h3>3. Vitruvi Stone — Best Design</h3>
<p>Crafted from ceramic and housed in a hand-finished stone vessel, the Vitruvi Stone embodies understated luxury. The ultrasonic technology produces a fine, cool mist, and the wooden lid doubles as a coaster.</p>
<h2 id="sec-4">Buying Guide</h2>
<p><strong>Ultrasonic vs. Nebulizing:</strong> Ultrasonic uses water and vibration — quiet, affordable, easy to clean. Nebulizing uses air pressure for pure oil dispersion without water, producing more potent fragrance but requiring more maintenance.</p>
<p><strong>Room size:</strong> Match diffuser capacity to room size. 100ml for bedrooms, 300ml+ for living rooms.</p>
<h2 id="sec-5">FAQs</h2>
<h3>How much essential oil should I use?</h3>
<p>3-5 drops per 100ml of water. Stronger scents need fewer drops; lighter scents may need 5-6.</p>
<h3>Can I leave my diffuser running overnight?</h3>
<p>Yes, if it has auto-shutoff. Run on intermittent mode and ensure the room is ventilated.</p>
<h2 id="sec-6">Final Thoughts</h2>
<div style="background:linear-gradient(135deg,#1A1A1A 0%,#2A2A2A 100%);color:white;padding:2rem;border-radius:12px;margin-top:2rem"><p style="font-family:'Playfair Display',serif;font-size:1.5rem;font-weight:700;margin:0 0 0.75rem 0;color:#C9A962">Our Recommendation</p><p style="margin:0;line-height:1.8">The <strong>URPOWER 2nd Edition</strong> at $26 is the best value. For larger spaces, the <strong>ASAKUKI Premium</strong> at $40 is outstanding. For design, the <strong>Vitruvi Stone</strong> at $80 is worth the investment.</p></div>
